{"name":"Polo Pony","hex":"#d09258","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"polo pony","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A horse used in the game of polo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/polo_pony"}],"entries":[{"title":"Polo pony","blocks":[{"text":"A polo pony is a horse used in the game of polo. They may be of any breed or combination of breeds, though many have a significant amount of Thoroughbred breeding. They are called \"ponies\", but that is a reference to their agile type rather than their size; almost all are horse-sized. They require considerable training and ongoing conditioning, and because each rider requires at least two horses in a single match, this can be a considerable expense. When playing, polo ponies have their manes roached and tails braided so that there is no danger of being tangled in the mallet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Polo_070922_16.jpg/330px-Polo_070922_16.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polo_pony","wikidata":"Q3064347"},{"title":"Polo","blocks":[{"text":"Polo is a stick and ball game that is played on horseback as a traditional field sport, and is one of the oldest known team sports in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Varsity_Polo_2013.jpg/330px-Varsity_Polo_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polo","wikidata":"Q134211"},{"title":"Pony","blocks":[{"text":"A pony is a type of small horse, usually under a specific height at full maturity. Ponies often have thicker coats, manes and tails, compared to larger horses, and proportionally shorter legs, wider barrels, heavier bone, thicker necks and shorter heads. In modern use, breed registries and horse shows may define a pony as measuring at the withers below a certain height; height limits varying from about 14 hands to 14.3 hands. Some distinguish between horse or pony based on its breed or phenotype, regardless of its height. The word pony derives from the old French poulenet, a diminutive of poulain meaning foal, a young, immature horse. A full-sized horse may sometimes be called a pony as a term of endearment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Gracie-rhs2005.jpg/330px-Gracie-rhs2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pony","wikidata":"Q188828"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/Polo_pony_docked.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/Polo_pony_docked.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Docked and banged tail on a polo pony, photographed between 1910 and 1915","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolo_pony_docked.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Polo_pony_taped.jpg/500px-Polo_pony_taped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Polo_pony_taped.jpg/500px-Polo_pony_taped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern polo pony's tail prepared for competition","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolo_pony_taped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Polo_game_from_poem_Guy_u_Chawgan.jpg/500px-Polo_game_from_poem_Guy_u_Chawgan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Polo_game_from_poem_Guy_u_Chawgan.jpg/500px-Polo_game_from_poem_Guy_u_Chawgan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Persian miniature from the poem Guy-o Chawgân (\"the Ball and the Polo-mallet\") during the Safavid dynasty of Persia, showing courtiers on horseback playing polo, 1546 CE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolo_game_from_poem_Guy_u_Chawgan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Polo_-_Liao_dinasztia%2C_K%C3%ADna.png/500px-Polo_-_Liao_dinasztia%2C_K%C3%ADna.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Polo_-_Liao_dinasztia%2C_K%C3%ADna.png/500px-Polo_-_Liao_dinasztia%2C_K%C3%ADna.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APolo_-_Liao_dinasztia%2C_K%C3%ADna.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg/500px-Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg/1280px-Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg/500px-Naghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Naqsh-e Jahan Square in Isfahan, Iran, is the site of a medieval royal polo field[25]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANaghshe_Jahan_Square_Isfahan_modified.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Georgians_playing_Polo_by_Castelli.jpg/500px-Georgians_playing_Polo_by_Castelli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Georgians_playing_Polo_by_Castelli.jpg/500px-Geor